   ALIGNMENT USING margin-left
   =========================================================

   Using the same margin-left value on multiple elements
   aligns them uniformly from the left side, creating a
   consistent vertical line.

   This helps keep layouts neat and readable, especially
   for lists, labels, and grouped content.

   Example:


.item {
    margin-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
}

<div class="item">First item</div>
<div class="item">Second item</div>
<div class="item">Third item</div>
